From 1ae171b48bb2109603a138e5059a6ade5ffbc2d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zak Wilson <zak.wilson@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 14:37:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] A field of a union member is a place; no cap on the number of
 macros

Two fixes found by the nuc-lua port.

`(set! (((uv 'u) 'open) 'next) n)`, Lua's `uv->u.open.next = n` with `u` a
union, was refused as a store into a temporary: place-value-type followed a
field only through a struct, so a union member's field had no type and was
emitted as a value. It follows a union too now (nuc-lua ISSUE-032;
s21-field-of-union-member-place).

The 257th defmacro of a compilation died with "macro table full". The cap
guarded the original C implementation's fixed array; g-macros is a growable
Vector, so the check is gone (nuc-lua ISSUE-033; s21-many-macros).

Gate: nuctests 1742 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped; bootstrap fixed point holds.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CsC8i2S7yJAHSpzRaddMj3
